From 323efb42e0b643e9d60b93c5839ef86876b6fb85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 77ph <tk@itarragon.net>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:21:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] test(operator): hermetic solution loop with a
 Kernel-owned service Safe

full-loop-kernel-owner.test.ts runs the same production loop as
full-loop.test.ts on the committed snapshot -- bootstrap, claim, execute,
deliver, solution settlement -- after moving the service Safe's ownership
from the agent EOA to a Kernel (ERC-4337) account, with the venue's Safe
transactions sent through kernelSafeBroadcasterFactory / agent-signer. It
also checks that each of the three loop transactions is a UserOperation of
the Kernel through the EntryPoint, and that Safe.addOwnerWithThreshold
through the Kernel is refused by the account's mandate.

The ERC-4337 side (EntryPoint v0.7, Kernel v3.3 + factory, TPM_sign's
P-256 modules and AgentPolicy, Solady's P-256 verifier) is installed with
anvil_setCode from a committed runtime-bytecode fixture: no live RPC.
startDaemon gains an optional safeBroadcaster.

Skipped unless TPM_SIGN_AGENT_SIGNER (the CLI) and TPM_SIGN_KEYS (an agent
config naming the agent key) are set; the agent key may be hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
